  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Fourteen men walked into the Florida sky and never returned. On December 5, 1945, five TBM Avenger torpedo bombers lifted off from Fort Lauderdale for a routine training mission.",
        "visual_query": "vintage military torpedo bomber aircraft",
        "visual_fallback": "old airplane flight"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Hours later, radio operators caught a chilling distress call. The flight leader reported that both of his compasses had failed, and nothing looked familiar below them.",
        "visual_query": "historic cockpit instrument panel",
        "visual_fallback": "cockpit gauges"
      },
      {
        "narration": "As the squadron flew in widening circles over the open ocean, darkness set in. But the mystery deepened when a rescue seaplane sent to find them vanished in a fiery explosion.",
        "visual_query": " stormy atlantic ocean horizon",
        "visual_fallback": "dark ocean waves"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Investigators piecing together the tragedy discovered the likely answer. Disoriented by navigational errors and severe weather, the squadron simply ran out of fuel and ditched at sea.",
        "visual_query": "navigator studying aviation map",
        "visual_fallback": "vintage map desk"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Shifting Atlantic currents and deep trenches ensured the planes vanished forever, leaving behind only an enduring aviation legend.",
        "visual_query": "deep blue ocean abyss",
        "visual_fallback": "deep ocean water"
      }
